    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's what happened and what I changed:\n\n## Problem\nThe `--ci` flag was not being passed through from the `frai` CLI to the `frai-gate` CLI when running `frai gate init --ci`. This was because:\n- The `--ci` flag is defined at the program level (line 605 of frai-cli)\n- When Commander.js parsed the command, it consumed the `--ci` flag at the program level before the gate subcommand handler could access it\n- The gate subcommand's action handler only received the positional arguments (`[\"init\"]`), not the flags\n\n## Solution\nI modified the gate command handler to directly use `process.argv` to capture all arguments after the \"gate\" keyword, ensuring that flags like `--ci` are passed through to the frai-gate CLI:\n\n```typescript\n// Find the \"gate\" index in process.argv and get everything after it\n// This ensures all flags (like --ci) are passed through to frai-gate\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : (args ?? []);\n```\n\n## Verification\nAfter rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, I tested the command and confirmed:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created (previously missing)\n- \u2705 The workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration\n\nThe fix is complete and tested.",
